# Keep the build context small, and — critically — never copy the host's node_modules or built
# artifacts into the image. The host's native modules (better-sqlite3) are built for the host OS and
# would break inside the Linux image; the image installs and builds its own.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
out
**/out
*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.github
.githooks
.DS_Store

# Local data and dev scratch that has no business in an image.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
blobs/

# Secrets and operator data (SIB2-205). The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, the hosted runbook puts `.env` and
# `backups/` in this directory, and a layer is forever (and the runbook pushes images to registries).
# Nothing below is needed to build the image. tests/arch/dockerignore.test.ts holds this list.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
backups/
**/backups/
deploy/
tools/runpod/
*.pem
*.key
*.age
*.sql
*.sql.gz
.claude/
